<DocLayout title="Privacy policy" description="Kitroid keeps your data on your own device. Nothing is sent to Kitroid.">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 16 November 2026</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>
    Kitroid tools run entirely in your web browser. <strong>Your business data stays on your own device</strong>
    (phone, tablet or computer). Kitroid has no servers that store your data, does not collect personal information,
    and cannot see, recover or delete your data.
  </p>
  <p lang="km">
    ឧបករណ៍ Kitroid ដំណើរការទាំងស្រុងនៅក្នុងកម្មវិធីរុករករបស់អ្នក។ ទិន្នន័យអាជីវកម្មរបស់អ្នកនៅតែលើឧបករណ៍ផ្ទាល់ខ្លួនរបស់អ្នក។
    Kitroid គ្មានម៉ាស៊ីនមេរក្សាទុកទិន្នន័យរបស់អ្នកទេ មិនប្រមូលព័ត៌មានផ្ទាល់ខ្លួន ហើយមិនអាចមើល ស្តារ ឬលុបទិន្នន័យរបស់អ្នកបានទេ។
  </p>

  <h2>What is stored, and where</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Data you enter in the tools (POS items, prices, photos and sales; income and expenses; customers; savings circles; calculator inputs) is stored in your browser's private storage on your device.</li>
    <li>A few device preferences (language, last backup time) are kept in your browser's local storage.</li>
    <li>Clearing your browser data, uninstalling the app or losing the device deletes this data unless you made a backup.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Backups</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Drive (optional):</strong> if you choose "Connect Google Drive", you sign in with your own Google account
      and allow Kitroid the <code>drive.file</code> permission. This lets the app create backup files in your Drive and read
      only the files it created. Backups are sent directly from your browser to Google. Kitroid never receives them, your
      Google password, or your access token. You can remove access at any time at
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Folder or download:</strong> backup files are saved to a location you choose on your device.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Kitroid's use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>Google user data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>What Kitroid accesses:</strong> only with your permission, the <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file</code> scope:
      the backup files Kitroid creates in your Google Drive (in the folder <em>My Drive / Kitroid</em>). Kitroid cannot see any other file
      in your Drive, and does not request your name, email address, contacts or any other Google data.</li>
    <li><strong>How it is used:</strong> to save your backups and to list, download and restore them on your devices, and (in POS, if you turn it on)
      to sync your own shop between your devices. Nothing else.</li>
    <li><strong>Storage and sharing:</strong> the access token stays in your browser's memory for about one hour and is never stored by or sent to
      Kitroid. Your Drive files are not shared with Kitroid or anyone else, not sold, and not used for advertising or to train AI models.</li>
    <li><strong>Deleting:</strong> you can delete the backup files in Google Drive at any time, and remove Kitroid's access at
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. Data on your device is deleted by clearing
      the site's data in your browser.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Third parties</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The website is hosted on GitHub Pages, which may keep standard server logs (such as IP addresses) when pages are downloaded.</li>
    <li>Google's sign-in script is loaded only when you choose to connect Google Drive.</li>
    <li>Kitroid uses no analytics, advertising or tracking.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about this policy: see the contact details on <a href="/">kitroid.com</a>.</p>
